# =========================================================================
# AI-Powered Alcohol Label Verification App - Environment Configuration Example
# =========================================================================
# Copy this file to '.env.local' inside the 'label-verification/' directory
# (Next.js reads env from the app directory, not the repo root).
#
# The application detects the provider based on which key is configured.
#
# IMPORTANT: Set ONLY the provider you intend to use. The backend routes to
# Claude whenever CLAUDE_API_KEY (or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) is present -- even a
# placeholder value -- so keep the Claude line COMMENTED OUT when using Gemini.
# =========================================================================

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Google Gemini API Configuration (Default)
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gemini 2.5 Flash is used for low-latency visual OCR extraction.
# Prefix: Key starts with 'AIza...'
# Obtain from: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Anthropic Claude API Configuration (Optional)
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude 3.5 Sonnet is used if a Claude key is provided (or if a key starting
# with 'sk-ant-' is entered in the UI Settings Panel).
# Uncomment ONLY if you want Claude instead of Gemini.
# CLAUDE_API_KEY=your_claude_api_key_here

# You can also use ANTHROPIC_API_KEY as an alias for CLAUDE_API_KEY:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_claude_api_key_here
